ADVERSARIAL BOUNDARY COVERAGE
- Whitespace, comma, semicolon, slash, and other non-username delimiters expose every subsequent malformed scheme-less userinfo candidate to redaction.
- A colon-prefixed safe diagnostic followed by whitespace is not misclassified as a username/password pair.
- First-pass and repeated redaction both retain the `db-reset:` prefix and already-redacted URL authorities.
- Lifecycle errors cover a preceding email-like authority followed by credential-bearing malformed endpoints under each explicit delimiter regression.
- All earlier configuration, serialization, URL, parser, fixture, DB/CLI, host, mapping, set, exception, format, delimiter, encoding, subclass, cycle/depth, and non-mutation probes remain covered.
